 ],
 "caption": "Deciding between an EC and a condo? Check these first. 🏙️\n\nRules: ECs are for Singaporean families within the income ceiling. Loans: new ECs are capped by MSR at 30% of income, condos by TDSR at 55% for all debts. On $16K a month, that's about $1M vs $1.8M of loan. On a $1.6M home: about $600K upfront for the EC vs $400K for the condo.\n\nNew ECs now have a 10 year MOP. ECs usually sit further out, and were traditionally 30 to 40% cheaper, which is why most EC owners made money. But what if a condo now costs about the same?\n\nTorn between the two? Comment COMPARE and we'll run both on your income 👇\n\nIllustration only: 4% stress test, 30 year loan, no other debts. Bank policies vary.",
 "hashtags": "#singaporeproperty #ecsg #executivecondo #condosg #tdsr #propertysg #tinysingapore"
}